<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="ws_7_3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>7.3 Practice Worksheet</title>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Let <m>f(x)=2x-1</m>, <m>g(x)=3x</m>, and <m>h(x)=x^2+1</m>. Find each of the following.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(g(x))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<md>
f(g(x)) \quad = \quad f(3x) \quad =  \quad 2(3x)-1 \quad = \quad 6x-1.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>h(g(x))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<md>
h(g(x)) \quad = \quad h(3x) \quad = \quad (3x)^2+1 \quad = \quad 9x^2+1.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>g(f(x))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<md>
g(f(x)) \quad = \quad g(2x-1) \quad = \quad 3(2x-1) \quad= \quad 6x-3.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(g(-3))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Option 1: Use the formula in part (a), plugging in <m>x=-3</m>. Then <m>f(g(-3)) = 6(-3)-1 = -19</m>.
</p>

<p>
Option 2: Evaluate the composition directly. Since <m>g(-3)=-9</m>, then <m>f(g(-3)) = f(-9) = -19</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(h(7))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Option 1: <em>Find the formula for <m>f(h(x))</m> if you want!</em>
</p>

<p>
Option 2: Evaluate the composition directly. Since <m>h(7) = 50</m>, then <m>f(h(7)) = f(50) = 2(50)-1=99</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(g(h(2)))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Option 1: <em>Find the formula for <m>f(g(h(x)))</m> if you want, but this is a LOT of work!</em>
</p>

<p>
Option 2: (Recommended!) Evaluate the composition directly, working inside-out. Note that <m>h(2)=2^2+1=5</m>. Then, <m>g(h(2)) = g(5) = 3(5)=15</m>. Lastly, <m>f(g(h(2))) = f(15) = 2(15)-1=29</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>




<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Let <m>f(x)=-3x+7</m> and <m>g(x)=2x^2-8</m>. Find the following.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(g(x))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<md>
<mrow>f(g(x)) \amp \quad =\quad f(2x^2-8) </mrow>
<mrow> \amp \quad = \quad -3(2x^2-8)+7 </mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad= \quad -6x^2+24+7 </mrow>
<mrow> \amp \quad = \quad -6x^2+31.</mrow>
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>g(f(x))</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<md>
g(f(x)) \quad = \quad  g(-3x+7) \quad = \quad 2(-3x+7)^2-8.
</md>
If you wish, you may find it advantageous to practice expanding this out:
</p>
<p>
<md>
<mrow>2(-3x+7)^2-8 \amp \quad = \quad 2(-3x+7)(-3x+7)-8</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 2(9x^2-21x-21x+49)-8</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 18x^2-84x+90</mrow>
</md>
</p>

</solution>
</task>


</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Identify functions <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m> to rewrite each of the following as a composition of the form <m>f(g(x))</m>.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=(4x+3)^2</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
A good rule of thumb is that we want to choose the inner function <mdash/> in this case <m>g(x)</m> <mdash/> to be the <q>function you would put a number into first</q> if you were evaluating the original function. So, here we could pick
<md>
g(x) = 4x+3, \qquad f(x)=x^2.
</md> To check this, note that
<md>
f(g(x)) \quad = \quad f(4x+3) \quad = \quad (4x+3)^2
</md> as desired.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=(x-1)^2+2(x-1)-8</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Here we can pick
<md>
g(x) = x-1, \qquad f(x)=x^2+2x-8.
</md> Verify on your own that this works by computing <m>f(g(x))</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\sqrt{x^2+7}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Here we can pick
<md>
g(x) = x^2+7, \qquad f(x)=\sqrt{x} .
</md> Another correct choice is to pick
<md>
g(x) = x^2, \qquad f(x) = \sqrt{x+7} .
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\dfrac{1}{3x^7+2}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Here we can pick
<md>
g(x) = 3x^7 + 2, \qquad f(x)=\frac{1}{x}.
</md> Another correct choice is to pick
<md>
g(x) = 3x^7, \qquad f(x) = \frac{1}{x+2}.
</md> Yet another is to use
<md>
g(x) = x^7, \qquad f(x)=\frac{1}{3x+2}.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>

</worksheet>